{
	"nodes":[
		{"id":"group-script","type":"group","x":4950,"y":40,"width":2990,"height":1120,"label":"Scripts UX"},
		{"id":"group-physic","type":"group","x":3350,"y":40,"width":1520,"height":1120,"label":"Physics Model"},
		{"id":"group-perfor","type":"group","x":8020,"y":40,"width":1030,"height":1550,"label":"Performance CI"},
		{"id":"group-episod","type":"group","x":20,"y":40,"width":1030,"height":1120,"label":"Episode State"},
		{"id":"group-simula","type":"group","x":1130,"y":40,"width":1030,"height":1120,"label":"Simulation API"},
		{"id":"group-loggin","type":"group","x":2240,"y":40,"width":1030,"height":1120,"label":"Logging Viz"},
		{"id":"legend","type":"text","text":"## Legend\n🔴 **Red** = To Do (ready)\n⬜ **Gray** = Blocked\n🟠 **Orange** = Doing\n🔵 **Cyan** = Ready to review\n🟢 **Green** = Done\n🟣 **Purple** = Proposed by agent","x":-540,"y":-310,"width":380,"height":230,"color":"0"},
		{"id":"canvas-warnings","type":"text","text":"## Warnings\n✓ None","x":-540,"y":-530,"width":380,"height":200,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"canvas-errors","type":"text","text":"## Errors\n✓ None","x":-540,"y":-750,"width":380,"height":200,"color":"1"},
		{"id":"5f202c6f","type":"text","text":"## LV-01 Promote wire diagnostics into the state contract\nMove wire_head_idx, wire_offset_mm, wire_material_positions_mm, and similar diagnostics into EDMState or a formal derived-signal registry instead of dynamic attribute writes.","x":2300,"y":80,"width":420,"height":220,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"eda4ab9f","type":"text","text":"## ES-03 Define episode-start defaults\nApply a single source of truth for initial generator, thermal, and electrical state so the first environment step does not depend on stale internals or mismatched per-module fallbacks.","x":570,"y":510,"width":420,"height":180,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"5733330b","type":"text","text":"## ES-04 Add reset isolation tests","x":80,"y":940,"width":420,"height":180,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"d8acd2df","type":"text","text":"## ES-02 Reset internal thermal and analysis state\nExpanded the module reset hooks so they now synchronize their mirrored EDMState fields as well as private caches. Ignition clears spark/current short state, dielectric clears debris and ion-channel state, mechanics clears servo carry-over, and wire clears the broken flag; regression coverage now verifies reset hooks work even on a dirty existing state object.","x":80,"y":510,"width":420,"height":180,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"aeddc858","type":"text","text":"## ES-01 Add module reset hooks\nIntroduce a formal reset API on ignition, wire, material, dielectric, and mechanics modules and call it from WireEDMEnv.reset so internal caches and episodic state cannot leak between runs.","x":80,"y":80,"width":420,"height":180,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"bc77ad27","type":"text","text":"## PM-01 Respect zero-valued generator commands\n\nReplaced truthy fallback checks in ignition with explicit None handling so 0V and 0us commands are preserved instead of snapping back to defaults. Added regression coverage that proves None still falls back while explicit zero-valued target voltage, ON time, and OFF time remain zero.","x":3410,"y":80,"width":420,"height":180,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"fb7f612e","type":"text","text":"## PM-02 Align module default discharge settings\n\nAligned ignition and material fallback handling around a shared crater-backed default current mode in the env. Reset and missing/unsupported state current modes now resolve to the same physical discharge mode, and regression tests cover both None and unsupported-mode fallbacks.","x":3410,"y":940,"width":420,"height":180,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"dfc7eb85","type":"text","text":"## PM-03 Make dt handling coherent\nAudit timestep scaling across ignition, wire, dielectric, and mechanics; either fully support variable dt or validate dt==1 and remove the misleading configurability.","x":3900,"y":80,"width":420,"height":180,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"ba618130","type":"text","text":"## PM-04 Clarify mechanics and constraint semantics\nDocumented position-control semantics in MechanicsModule docstring. Removed three orphaned EnvironmentConfig fields (max_wire_temperature, min_gap_for_operation, max_cutting_force) that were never enforced. Updated docs.","x":4390,"y":80,"width":420,"height":180,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"280b5854","type":"text","text":"## LV-04 Make analysis tracking opt-in and reset-safe\nGate crater-history and other analysis-only accumulators behind explicit configuration and make sure they reset cleanly between episodes.","x":2790,"y":940,"width":420,"height":180,"color":"1"},
		{"id":"370962f7","type":"text","text":"## PC-01 Remove duplicate wire state sync\n\nMake the NumPy wire arrays the single live representation for segment position, temperature, and damage, and stop synchronizing both those arrays and per-segment dataclass objects on every microstep unless a caller explicitly asks for a snapshot view. Keep the `EDMState` array outputs needed by logging and visualization stable, but treat `wire.segments` as a compatibility/debug surface instead of part of the hot simulation path. This should remove a large amount of Python bookkeeping, reduce per-step cost that scales with segment count, and make the optimization story clearer without changing the underlying physics. Main tradeoffs: external code that assumes `wire.segments` is always live may need a compatibility shim, lazy snapshot views can introduce stale-data bugs if the contract is unclear, and any reduction in `EDMState` syncing must preserve logger/export behavior.\n","x":5010,"y":80,"width":420,"height":180,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"d84a8af7","type":"text","text":"## LV-03 Add end-to-end logging smoke tests\nAdd NPZ/pack generation tests that assert dashboard-required fields exist and can be exported from a real environment run.","x":2300,"y":920,"width":420,"height":200,"color":"0"},
		{"id":"287c55df","type":"text","text":"## SA-01 Define observation contract\nDesign a real observation schema, populate observation_space, and document the intended public control-step interface versus internal microphysics stepping.","x":1190,"y":80,"width":420,"height":180,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"217e4253","type":"text","text":"## PC-03 Split fast and slow test lanes\nSeparate long stochastic physics tests from the default fast suite, add example and logging smoke tests, and keep CI runtime practical.","x":8080,"y":1370,"width":420,"height":180,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"b253d8f3","type":"text","text":"## PC-02 Accelerate thermal and damage hot paths\nCompiled the per-segment damage accumulation loop with Numba, precomputed the damage constants used every step, and removed the unused thermal-update kernel so wire.py has a single live thermal path. Benchmarked with scripts/profile_simulation.py at 50k steps / 2k warmup / 1 repeat: 0.20 mm mesh improved from 5710 to 32791 steps/s (5.74x) and 0.05 mm improved from 2045 to 30284 steps/s (14.81x) with matching crater count, mean wire temperature, and wire max damage. Simulation integration suite passed; broader env/reset suites still fail on unrelated pre-existing ignition/reset contract issues.","x":5010,"y":510,"width":420,"height":180,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"3a258c06","type":"text","text":"## SU-01 Repair example runner configs\nUpdate examples/quickstart.py and examples/run_simulation.py to use the current logger signal names and a working end-to-end export path.","x":5010,"y":940,"width":420,"height":180,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"27ab8b1b","type":"text","text":"## SU-03 Fix voltage sweep experiment semantics\nFixed voltage sweep semantics in experiments/voltage_sweep_speed_analysis.py: (1) generator_control.target_voltage now follows the swept setpoint (was hardcoded 80 V). (2) Thermal quench uses WireModuleParameters.base_convection_coefficient=1e8; removed no-op env.wire.h_conv. (3) Wire diameter set on EnvironmentConfig.wire_diameter=0.25 mm (was invalid wire_params.wire_diameter). (4) Plot/npz aligned with protocol: x-axis target voltage, dropped misleading SSoil/ssoll; npz no longer writes ssoll_values.","x":5500,"y":80,"width":420,"height":180,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"5f730cee","type":"text","text":"## SU-04 Normalize CLI output portability\nReplaced all non-ASCII glyphs in print() output across canvas-tool.py and experiment scripts with ASCII-safe equivalents: arrows -> ->, checkmarks -> [ok], crosses -> [FAIL], warning emoji -> [!], em dashes -> --, micro sign -> u, superscripts -> ^^, middle dots -> *.","x":5990,"y":80,"width":420,"height":180,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"aa2748ce","type":"text","text":"## PC-04 Make pytest work from a clean checkout\nAdded a pytest bootstrap in tests/conftest.py that prepends this checkout's src directory to sys.path so local tests import wedm from the fresh clone instead of a shadowing install or another checkout. Added tests/test_import_path.py as a regression guard that asserts wedm resolves from repo/src/wedm. Verified with plain pytest and no PYTHONPATH override: test_import_path, test_env_integration, test_reset_isolation, and the full suite all pass (52 passed).","x":8080,"y":80,"width":420,"height":180,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"4765e75c","type":"text","text":"## PC-05 Add repeatable simulation profiling harness\nAdded scripts/profile_simulation.py to benchmark the local src tree with defaults aligned to an active workload (12 um initial gap, 100k steps). The harness reports throughput, crater counts, module wall-time shares, cProfile hotspots, and optional JSON output for before/after comparisons. Baseline 100k-step run: about 4.8k steps/s at 0.2 mm segments and about 1.37k steps/s at 0.05 mm segments, with 1986 craters in both runs.","x":8570,"y":80,"width":420,"height":180,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"8ac634f4","type":"text","text":"## SA-02 Refactor public step contract\nMake every public step consume an action and return a valid observation and reward, even if the environment internally substeps physics for servo or discharge timing.","x":1190,"y":510,"width":420,"height":180,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"98a5aab4","type":"text","text":"## SA-03 Redesign current-mode action encoding\nReplace the current_mode Box(1..19) with an encoding that only represents supported crater-data modes so sampled actions are valid by construction.","x":1680,"y":80,"width":420,"height":180,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"0d1a98c9","type":"text","text":"## SA-04 Finalize RL semantics and compliance tests\nImplement non-placeholder reward and truncation semantics, then add Gym-style contract tests for reset/step formats, valid sampled actions, and wrapper compatibility.","x":1190,"y":940,"width":420,"height":180,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"2288b93e","type":"text","text":"## SU-02 Repair experiment logging workflows\nFix experiments/run_simulation.py and related animation entry points so their default logging modes run successfully without requiring --no-log.","x":5500,"y":940,"width":420,"height":180,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"b67be33f","type":"text","text":"## SU-05 Add example runner CLI overrides\nUpdated examples/run_simulation.py to prepend the local src directory to sys.path, added CLI flags for --segment-len and --wire-diameter, and refreshed the runner's logger signal list to match the current logger contract (gap_um and wire_max_damage instead of stale gap_width / wire_material_positions_mm). Verified with plain python examples/run_simulation.py and no PYTHONPATH override using a smoke command that set workpiece height 10 mm, segment length 0.5 mm, wire diameter 0.25 mm, current mode I7, and target voltage 47 V; the run wrote a sparc_pack_v1 NPZ archive successfully. Full pytest suite still passes (52 passed).","x":6480,"y":80,"width":420,"height":180,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"834ac61c","type":"text","text":"## SU-06 Fix example runner servo sign\nCorrect the gap-controller sign in examples/run_simulation.py so velocity control advances the wire when the gap is larger than the target, matching the mechanics semantics and the quickstart controller.","x":6970,"y":80,"width":420,"height":180,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"28761f84","type":"text","text":"## SU-07 Unify runner controller voltage semantics\nImplemented explicit runner controller semantics in examples/run_simulation.py and experiments/run_simulation.py. Both runners now expose --controller gap|voltage|fixed-servo, separate --generator-voltage from --target-avg-voltage, reject ambiguous legacy --target-voltage, and support fixed-servo commands. Verified with CLI smoke runs for voltage and fixed-servo modes plus pytest -q (56 passed).","x":7460,"y":80,"width":420,"height":180,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"4b9517d0","type":"text","text":"## LV-02 Repair logger and export contracts\nUpdate SimulationLogger validation, exporters, and dashboard pack metadata so visualization-required signals are supported without bypassing the type contract.","x":2300,"y":380,"width":420,"height":210,"color":"0"}
	],
